# Build output — see /Makefile. Nothing under here is a source file: dist/ holds
# everything a build produces, the product as a machine runs it and the files a
# person downloads, and .dev/ is that same shape made of symlinks, for running
# against the sources.
/dist/
/.dev/

# The runtime, downloaded from its own project rather than built here.
/.oak/

# What a local run leaves beside itself, wherever it runs from. Each module
# names its answers and its log after itself, and Oak keeps what belongs to
# every module in one of its own.
oak.conf
installer.conf
installer.conf.old
installer.log
installer.log.old
recovery.conf
recovery.conf.old
recovery.log
recovery.log.old

# Editors / OS noise
*.swp
.DS_Store
